      <title>Mystery over source of Ebola infection in Nigeria fuels concern about spread of virus</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/23/ebola-swiss-patient-nigeria-dr-congo-concerns-virus-spread</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Switzerland says patient is wife of Swiss diplomat and believed to have contracted virus while travelling in Uganda&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Health officials across Africa are racing to determine how Nigeria’s first Ebola patient ⁠in more than a decade ⁠became infected, amid fears ​the outbreak could spread further after reaching a fourth African country.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Swiss foreign ministry said on Friday the patient in Nigeria, the Ugandan-born wife of a Swiss diplomat based in Abuja, had not travelled to the Democratic Republic of ⁠Congo, where the outbreak was first detected in mid-May before spreading to Uganda, Kenya and now Nigeria. The woman was believed to have contracted Ebola while travelling with her husband in Uganda, the ministry added.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/23/ebola-swiss-patient-nigeria-dr-congo-concerns-virus-spread"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
