<item>
      <title>Lewis Hamilton aims to extend career till early 2030s so he can race in African Grand Prix</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/22/lewis-hamilton-aims-to-extend-career-till-early-2030s-so-he-can-race-in-african-grand-prix</link>
      <description>&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;41-year-old set on ‘dream to be able to race in Africa’&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rwanda to host despite criticism of human rights record&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lewis Hamilton has said he hopes to remain racing in Formula One until he can take part in the African Grand Prix which is &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/13/f1-returns-to-africa-for-first-time-since-1993-with-10-year-rwanda-deal-from-early-2030s"&gt;set to take place in Rwanda in the 2030s&lt;/a&gt;. The seven-time world champion believes it is right that F1 is to hold a race there despite criticism of the country’s human rights record.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Last week F1 confirmed Rwanda was to host the African Grand Prix having concluded a 10-year agreement for the meeting on a purpose-built circuit, with the first race set for the early 2030s. It is lined up to be held on a circuit in Bugesera, 25 miles south of the capital, Kigali, which has yet to be constructed and marks a return to the African continent for the first time since it last held a race at Kyalami, South Africa in 1993.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/22/lewis-hamilton-aims-to-extend-career-till-early-2030s-so-he-can-race-in-african-grand-prix"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
