      <title>Lula wins fourth term as Brazil president after historic upset over far-right Flávio Bolsonaro</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/lula-wins-brazil-election</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Leftist incumbent Lula says unprecedented comeback was a ‘defeat for denialism’ as Bolsonaro refuses to accept election result&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/oct/25/brazil-election-runoff-live-updates-flavio-bolsonaro-lula"&gt;Lula wins election in stunning comeback – live updates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/luiz-inacio-lula-da-silva"&gt;Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva&lt;/a&gt;, the &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/luiz-inacio-lula-da-silva"&gt;Brazilian&lt;/a&gt; president, has staged a dramatic &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/27/viscerally-dedicated-to-social-issues-behind-lulas-drive-to-win-final-term-in-brazils-crunch-election"&gt;election fightback&lt;/a&gt;, defeating his far-right opponent, &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/fl-vio-bolsonaro"&gt;Flávio Bolsonaro&lt;/a&gt;, to claim a historic fourth term in power.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;With 100% of votes counted the 80-year-old leftist received 51.79% of the vote to his 45-year-old rival’s 48.21%.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/lula-wins-brazil-election"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
