      <description>&lt;p&gt;Super typhoon weakening but large parts of Taiwan, including Taipei, still mostly closed and flights cancelled&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Typhoon Champi swept past Taiwan on Saturday killing one person, injuring more than 500, and uprooting trees and severing power as it weakened and ⁠headed north toward ⁠the ​Chinese coast.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Earlier classified as a super typhoon and one of the strongest storms in the ⁠Pacific this year, Champi was still packing gusts of about 126km per hour (78 miles per hour) near its ⁠centre, according to Taiwan’s Central Weather Administration (CWA).&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/24/typhoon-champi-kills-one-and-injures-more-than-500-in-taiwan-as-it-heads-to-china"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
